<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Reasoning Complexity Rating Prompt</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A1.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ A.1 Reasoning Complexity Rating Prompt ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ DeReason: A Difficulty-Aware Curriculum Improves Decoupled SFT-then-RL Training for General Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> presents the prompt template used to assess the reasoning complexity of questions on a 1–5 scale.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T3" class="ltx_table"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.T3.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="886.77" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 886.77" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,886.77) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#606060;" fill="#606060" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 880.87 C 0 884.13 2.64 886.77 5.91 886.77 L 544.09 886.77 C 547.36 886.77 550 884.13 550 880.87 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 862.66 L 548.03 862.66 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.44 871.26)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.13em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="458.43"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.T3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.13em;">
<span id="A1.T3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Reasoning Complexity Rating Prompt</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.44 14.52)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.29em;--ltx-fo-height:60.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.22em;font-size:10pt;" height="841.76" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 838.69)" width="502.15"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.T3.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.29em;">
<span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Please rate the reasoning complexity of the given question using the scale below.
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:4.0pt;">
Question: &lt;question&gt; {question} &lt;/question&gt;
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:6.0pt;">
</span></span>
<span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">ReasoningRequired Scale:
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:4.0pt;"><span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_medium">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1 - Minimal:<span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_medium"> Direct recall or single-step lookup
<br class="ltx_break"> • Answer is immediately retrievable from memory/knowledge
<br class="ltx_break"> • No logical steps or decomposition needed
<br class="ltx_break"> • Example: ‘‘What is the capital of France?’’
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:4.0pt;">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2 - Simple:<span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_medium"> One or two logical steps
<br class="ltx_break"> • Requires basic inference or straightforward calculation
<br class="ltx_break"> • Single relationship or comparison
<br class="ltx_break"> • Example: ‘‘If apples cost $2 and you have $5, how many can you buy?’’
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:4.0pt;">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3 - Moderate:<span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_medium"> Multiple steps with clear structure
<br class="ltx_break"> • Requires 3--5 logical steps or simple decomposition
<br class="ltx_break"> • May need to combine 2--3 concepts or rules
<br class="ltx_break"> • Example: ‘‘How would inflation affect consumer spending patterns?’’
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:4.0pt;">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4 - Complex:<span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_medium"> Multi-step analysis with dependencies
<br class="ltx_break"> • Requires 5--8 logical steps with intermediate conclusions
<br class="ltx_break"> • Need to track multiple variables or relationships
<br class="ltx_break"> • May require considering trade-offs or constraints
<br class="ltx_break"> • Example: ‘‘Design an algorithm to optimize traffic flow in a city’’
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:4.0pt;">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">5 - Deep:<span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_medium"> Extensive reasoning with abstract thinking
<br class="ltx_break"> • Requires 8+ logical steps with nested reasoning
<br class="ltx_break"> • Must synthesize multiple frameworks or domains
<br class="ltx_break"> • Involves hypothesis formation, proof, or complex problem decomposition
<br class="ltx_break"> • Example: ‘‘Prove the halting problem is undecidable’’
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:6.0pt;">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Consider:
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_medium"> - Number of logical steps required
<br class="ltx_break"> - Depth of decomposition needed
<br class="ltx_break"> - Dependencies between reasoning steps
<br class="ltx_break"> - Need for intermediate conclusions
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:6.0pt;">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Output format:
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.pic1.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_medium">Analysis: [Analyze the question step by step, identifying: (1) what knowledge/operations are needed, (2) how many logical steps are involved, (3) what dependencies exist between steps, (4) which scale level best matches these requirements]
<br class="ltx_break">ReasoningRequired: [1--5]
</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Prompt template for rating the reasoning complexity of questions. The <span id="A1.T3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{question}</span> placeholder is replaced with the target question at inference time.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
</article>
